      "text": "**36/36** — all tasks pass. Final review of the changes before committing:\n\n- **#212** `paths.resolve()`: relative paths now join against `base` (the project work dir), not `os.getcwd()`.\n- **#215** `retry.call_with_retry()`: retries transient errors (connection/timeout, and HTTP 408/429/5xx-style statuses) with exponential backoff capped at `MAX_DELAY`; non-transient errors raise immediately.\n- **#219** `router.py`: patterns are matched against lower-cased text, so `README|CHANGELOG|Documentation` and `DEPS.md|Dependenc` could never fire — now lower-case, and `docs` is recognised as a docs term.\n- **#224** `format.message()`: dropped the ASCII encode/decode round-trip; non-ASCII names pass through, still length-capped.\n- **#223** `guardrails.py`: full policy — task-level gating (routine categories allowed; sensitive categories like license/CI/rename/branch-protection and unclassified requests need approval), call-level gating (fs scoped to the two project roots, append-only writes to `team-shared`, `.git` modifications denied, system-path modifications refused, SSRF protection on `http.get`, fail-closed on unknown tools).",
